<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hōjō Sōun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1456">1456</a>–<a href="/years/1519">1519</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ise Moritoki, Ise Shinkurō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hōjō Sōun, born Ise Moritoki, was a minor shogunal official with ties to the Imagawa who helped settle their succession dispute in Suruga after 1476. In the 1490s he seized Izu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> castle, becoming one of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku</a> warlords. His son Ujitsuna adopted the Hōjō name, founding the Later Hōjō, who dominated eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hojo-soun.jpg" alt="Hōjō Sōun" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soun_Hojo_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
